<p>
  <b>mbem</b> is a boundary element method for 3-D linear elasticity built on
  <i>mollified</i> Green's functions. Following Cortez, the point force is
  replaced by a smooth blob of width &epsilon; and the elastostatic equations
  are then solved <i>exactly</i> &mdash; so the kernels are singular nowhere and
  still satisfy a PDE, which softening the kernel by hand would not. A fault
  therefore has a finite width &epsilon;, and stress is defined on the fault
  itself, where classical dislocation theory returns a value that ordinary
  integration does not define. Each triangle's contribution is integrated in
  closed form, which decouples &epsilon; from the mesh size <i>h</i>.
</p>
